    "definitions": {
      "short": "enjoyment",
      "usage": "delight, pleasure.",
      "full": "H8191. shaashuim [ שַׁעֲשֻׁעִים ], שׁוּעִים - noun [masculine] plural intensive delight (Ba NB 206 ); — absolute שׁוּעִים - Jer 31:20 ; Prov 8:30 ; suffix שׁוּעָיו - Isa 5:7 , usually שֻׁעַי - Prov 8:31 ; Psa 119:24 , שֻׁעָ֑י - 119:77 3 t.; — delight , in phrase שׁ ׳נְטַע Isa 5:7 the planting of his delight (in which he took delight), so שׁ ׳יֶלֶד Jer 31:20 (|| יַקִּיר בֵּן ); ׳שׁ אֶתֿ Prov 8:31 my delight (was) with the sons of men; elsewhere = object of delight , of wisdom 8:30 ; God's law, etc., Psa 119:24 ; 119:77 ; 119:92 ; 119:143 ; 119:174 .",
